module pwc.mojom;

import "chrome/browser/pwc/pwc_features.mojom";

// The elevated-capability bridge exposed only to a fully-qualified privileged
// main frame. "Fully qualified" means the requesting frame is the primary
// main frame of a PrivilegedWebContents, its document is committed over HTTPS
// to a capability origin per the component policy (see
// //chrome/browser/pwc/pwc_component_policy.h), and its process actually
// received origin isolation.
//
// The interface is intentionally empty: the production capability surface is
// a feature-team follow-on, and the security-relevant part is not any method
// but the *gate* on who may bind the interface at all -- enforced
// browser-side in //chrome/browser/pwc/pwc_api_binder.* and, as defense in
// depth, guarded with [RuntimeFeature] below so the interface is not even
// registered when PrivilegedWebContents is disabled. Tests observe a
// successful vs. refused bind via Remote::FlushForTesting() plus
// connectivity, so no test-only method ships here.
[RuntimeFeature=pwc.mojom.features.kPrivilegedWebContents]
interface PrivilegedBridge {};
